;; Stop-test regression (fidelity row SA11): the first rule's union builds (F (a)) on
;; both sides, so its two sides already share a class and the action reported no change.
;; The round minted a node and the loop still stopped on `changes == 0`, so the second
;; rule never matched (F (a)) and the check failed, naive and semi-naive. The loop now
;; also compares the graph's size stamp (node count, class count) around the actions.
(datatype E (F E) (a) (b))
(let t (a))
(rule ((a)) ((union (F (a)) (F (a)))))
(rule ((F x)) ((union (F x) (b))))
(run 10)
(check-eq (F (a)) (b))
